WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.040
Good morning Hank, it's Monday

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.500
Hank it's no secret that the three most viewed videos on the vlogbrothers channel

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.340
feature, in order, giraffe sex, giraffe sex, and giraffe sex.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.180
And, yet, Hank, it recently occurred to me that in spite of all of this,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.980
we have never actually made a video about...

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.440
Giraffe sex.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.020
A shortcoming I intend to rectify today.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.660
So, Hank, not to call you out, but the other day

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.200
on twitter, you tweeted an image that you designed.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.280
Now, Hank, let's put aside the question of why you,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.780
a busy professional, spend your free time coming up with

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.400
cute images of giraffe love, THIS would make a great t-shirt, and so

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.840
it IS a great t-shirt.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.320
Hank, nerdfighters, that shirt is available for preorder now at dftba.com

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.240
link in the dooblydoo!

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.740
But anyway, Hank, you illustration of giraffe love may be adorable

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.900
but it completely belies the truth about giraffe mating

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.900
which is that it is profoundly

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.800
...

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.260
non-romantic.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.640
To begin with, Hank, giraffes are extremely promiscuous

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.460
and when I say "extremely promiscuous"

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.360
I mean they rarely mate with the same person twice

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.580
In fact they don't mate with people at all,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.600
they mate with giraffes.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.380
Although that reminds me of a Yahoo answers question that I wanted to read to you

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.420
"Are male giraffes gay homosexual? I heard that they were

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.240
and if they are, would they be interested in male humans?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.200
My friend was asking and I said I would find out for him."

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.920
Hank, pardon me for a moment, I need to use the desk really quickly.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.600
Uuuuuggghhh! Headdesk!

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.320
Ohhhhhh, the internet, what disturbing question won't you ask?

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.940
Well, Hank, to answer that question on behalf of someone's non-existent friend

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.640
almost all male giraffes are bisexual.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.060
In fact, researchers believe that 90% of total giraffe sex

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.580
is male giraffes having sex with male giraffes

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.460
and that 1% of total giraffe sex is females having sex with females.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.280
Meaning that just about 9% of giraffe sex is heterosexual.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.440
And that's really no wonder, Hank, because their heterosexual sex is...

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.980
gwebechabah

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.780
So, Hank, I present to you the majestic giraffe.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.320
Stop looking at me that way, I know your secrets.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.540
Giraffe mating involves a process called "flaymen"

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.560
or possibly "flehmen"

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.060
I don't know how to pronounce it and I don't want to learn.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.260
Basically, male giraffes don't really like hooking up with female giraffes

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:05.080
unless they're ovulating, so to find out if they're ovulating

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.940
they use their faces to smack

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.120
the female giraffes in the bottom,

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.040
which causes the female giraffes to pee.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.600
If they happen to like the male giraffe they'll pee a bunch.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.420
And then the male giraffe drinks the pee to find out if it tastes like it's time to party.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.580
Hank I will remind you I am not the pervert here

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.120
I am just reporting the facts.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.760
He's the pervert!

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.980
Then, if the pee smells right and the lady's still into it,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.920
there's a courtship process which mostly involves

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.560
the male giraffe trying to hump the female giraffe

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.440
and the female giraffe running away.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.100
Until finally, coitus occurs, lasting up to

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:37.760
...

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.660
several seconds.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.780
Then, the mommy giraffes are pregnant for

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.100
Four. Hundred. Freaking. Days!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.420
No wonder they try to run away.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.840
And the male giraffe just goes on his merry way,

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.520
hooking up with dudes, and...

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:49.600
...smackin'...

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.540
...pee outta girls.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.140
...

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.680
I wish I were making this up.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.000
So anyway, Hank, the long and short of it is

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.760
that the animal kingdom is rarely as romantic as we'd like it to be.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.660
But there is one super cute thing about giraffes,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.920
as seen in your image, they neck a lot.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.420
And for a long time, biologists thought this was a way of fighting

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.080
but it turns out that while it is sometimes a way of fighting,

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.780
it's also kind of a way of hugging :).

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.120
So the shirt isn't a "lie" it's just an oversimplification

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.220
Like, some day when Henry asks me,

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.460
"How is it that baby giraffes come into the world?"

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.520
I will put on the shirt, and I will say,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.240
"Henry, this shirt was designed by your uncle, Hank

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.780
to answer that very question."

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.640
As this helpful diagram shows, as giraffes neck,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.580
there's a heart that forms in the space between their necks

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.220
and that heart,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.040
*whisper* is a baby giraffe!

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.280
Thus ends our introduction to giraffe mating habits

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.100
There's a link to Hank's t-shirt in the dooblydoo

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.320
Hank, thank you for designing that, I always forget that

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.020
you're so... talented.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.460
I know that sounds stupid but every time I see something you've designed

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.300
I always think, "wow, Hank is pretty...

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:48.900
...you know...

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.300
...good at stuff."

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.780
That's about as close as brothers get to complimenting each other

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.960
Hank, I'll see you on Wednesday!

